Subject: [PATCH] Keep dequantizer precision in the C IDCT

JPEGFixQuantD folds the AAN scale into the quantizers as (q * scale) >> 12,
which leaves 2 fraction bits. A high-quality file has quantizers of 1-2, and
there the high-frequency entries lose up to all of their value (q = 1 with the
F(7,7) scale of 0.30 becomes 0). Gray text and line art then come out up to a
few levels off on every pixel near an edge, against libjpeg.

- JPEGFixQuantD keeps up to 4 more fraction bits (ucQuantShift), as many as
  keep every entry in 16 bits. The C column pass and the DC-only shortcut shift
  them out after the multiply, so the intermediate range does not change. The
  SSE and NEON column passes multiply 16-bit lanes and keep the old 2 bits.
- The final >> 5 truncated, so output was on average half a level dark; the
  DC term now carries the rounding, in the IDCT and the DC-only shortcut alike.
- The 1/4-scale shortcut summed the AAN-scaled F(0,1), F(1,0) and F(1,1) as if
  they were the weights of a 4x4 mean, 1.5x and 2.3x too heavy; it was only
  hidden by the truncation above. They are now weighed by 0.653 and 0.427.

---
